      "contextFingerprint": "3f72100a5969b9209475ebc1fba522b5623d5022a7e3f179e5748c929ebeea73",
      "sourceText": "| 示例 | 讲了什么 | 新出现的语法 | 为什么这样写 | 注意事项 |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| 示例 1 | optional 返回查找结果 | `return i;` / `return std::nullopt;`、`if(opt)`、`*opt`、`value_or()` | optional 让\"没有值\"成为正常返回，语义清晰 | 解引用 `*opt` 前要确保有值 |\n| 示例 2 | optional 表示转换失败 | `try/catch` 包装 + optional | 把异常转换成空 optional，调用者更易处理 | 也可以用 `std::from_chars`（C++17）更高效 |\n| 示例 3 | optional 作为成员变量 | `std::optional<std::string>` 成员 | \"可选字段\"用 optional 比用 magic value（如 -1）更清晰 | optional 本身占用额外空间（T 的大小 + bool + padding） |",
      "translatedText": "| Example | What was discussed | Newly introduced syntax | Why it is written this way | Notes |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| Example 1 | optional returns the lookup result | `return i;` / `return std::nullopt;`、`if(opt)`、`*opt`、`value_or()` | optional makes \"no value\" a normal return, with clear semantics | Before dereferencing `*opt` , ensure there is a value |\n| Example 2 | optional indicates conversion failure | `try/catch` wrapping \\+ optional | Convert exceptions into an empty optional, making it easier for callers to handle | You can also use `std::from_chars` (C++17), which is more efficient |\n| Example 3 | optional as a member variable | `std::optional<std::string>` member | For \"optional fields\", using optional is clearer than using magic values (such as \\-1) | optional itself takes extra space (size of T \\+ bool \\+ padding) |",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 278,
        "outputTokens": 169,
        "costUsd": 0.000287
      }
